      "type": "item",
      "section": "Compute, chips & infrastructure",
      "headline": "Nvidia reports $115.8 billion in quarterly revenue, up 103%, and guides to $130 billion with no China compute revenue",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "Nvidia reported, in its first earnings call since Jensen Huang resigned." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Revenue of $115.8 billion for the quarter ended October 25th, up 103 percent year over year. Data centre revenue of $107.6 billion, up 110 percent. Earnings of $2.70 per diluted share on a GAAP basis." },
